// ===========================================================================
// ROUND 116, BUG 11 -- WHERE A RUN SHEET PUTS ITS FEET.
//
//   "Body type 2 fully armored running animation appears glitched, it's not
//    accurate to the animation."
//
// Every armoured run has been drawn with ONE origin since round 5 --
// RUN_FOOT_X / RUN_FOOT_Y in playerAnim.js, 45.75 and 78 of a 92-pixel cell,
// measured off the bare body's own run and then assumed of the twenty-eight
// sheets that came after it. `tools/scan_run_anchors.py` measures each sheet
// instead: the foot is the mean x of the lowest opaque row of every cell.
// Twenty-seven of them land within half a pixel of each other. One does not:
//
//   sword_axe_run.png   footX 33.6, footY 63.2   -- 12 px left, 15 px high
//
// So a body-type-2 character in full plate with a sword in one hand and an
// axe in the other stood correctly, and the moment they moved they slid a
// third of a tile sideways and floated a half-tile off the ground, then
// snapped back when they stopped. It is the only combo in the game with its
// own dedicated run export, which is why it is the only one that could be
// exported to a different anchor than the rest and why nothing else shows it.
//
// MEASURED, NOT NUDGED. The numbers here are what the scanner prints, so
// re-running it after an art drop either agrees with this table or names the
// sheet that changed. The dead round-33 `cut_*` cutout sources are off-anchor
// too and are deliberately absent: nothing loads them (grep finds no
// reference in src/), so an entry for them would be a claim about art the
// game does not draw.
export const ARMORED_RUN_ANCHOR = {
  sword_axe: { footX: 33.6, footY: 63.2 },
};

// How long ONE STRIDE takes, in milliseconds, whatever a sheet's frame count.
//
// The second half of bug 11, and the same sheet. Every armoured run has eight
// frames a direction except `sword_axe`, which has four, and the stepper ran
// every one of them at a flat 90ms -- so that combo's cycle finished in 360ms
// against everybody else's 720 and the character ran on the spot at double
// tempo. A stride is a stride: the CYCLE is the fixed quantity and the frames
// divide it.
export const ARMORED_RUN_CYCLE_MS = 720;
